---
/**
 * THE ADOPTION PAGE, BROUGHT BACK WITH A DIFFERENT SCOPE.
 *
 * `/for-schools/` was withdrawn because it was a pitch written before the
 * product had been shown to a single teacher, and a pitch that has never met
 * its audience is a guess (23.4). What brings it back is that the offer is
 * now a real one: a demonstration tenant a teacher can open unaided, and a
 * pilot that means one program rather than a district.
 *
 * It is deliberately written about what an organization *receives* and what
 * setting one up *involves*, both of which are facts about the software, and
 * not about what a teacher supposedly wants, which is still the part we do
 * not know. No counted claims, no named schools, nothing implying anybody has
 * adopted it.
 *
 * Platform only. A school running this does not need to be sold it.
 */
export const prerender = false;

import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import { activeOrg } from '../../lib/tenant';
import { platform } from '../../config/site';

const org = activeOrg(Astro);
if (!org.isPlatform) return Astro.redirect('/', 301);

const receives = [
  {
    title: 'Your own space',
    body:
      'An address of your own, your name on it, and your students, projects and records held apart from every other organization.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Programs, not one process',
    body:
      'A class, a club, a fair, a grant and a journal are separate programs with their own calendars, deliverables, roles and rules. A person may hold a role in more than one.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Roles that match who does what',
    body:
      'Students, student leaders, advisors and editors, each seeing what their role needs and nothing else. A student leader operates under a named adult.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A public record',
    body:
      'Completed work publishes to a showcase with stable addresses, stated authorship and citations, readable by anybody without an account.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="For organizations"
  description="Run a research program with its own calendar, roles and public record, hosted or self-hosted."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="For organizations"
    title="A research program you can actually run"
    lede="For schools, clubs, homeschool groups and fair associations that want a repeatable season rather than a rebuilt one."
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>What an organization receives</b><span>Four things</span></div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        {
          receives.map((r) => (
            <div class="card pad">
              <p class="t-lbl">{r.title}</p>
              <p class="t-sm" style="margin-top:9px">{r.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>Two ways to run it</b><span>Both supported</span></div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card pad">
          <p class="t-lbl">Hosted for you</p>
          <p class="t-sm" style="margin-top:9px">
            We operate the software. Your organization manages its own programs, its students
            and its records. This is what a volunteer-run club or fair association needs,
            because asking its board to become system administrators is not realistic.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card pad">
          <p class="t-lbl">Self-hosted</p>
          <p class="t-sm" style="margin-top:9px">
            The source is open and licensed from the first commit. An organization with its own
            infrastructure runs its own copy, holds its own students' data, and keeps operating
            regardless of what happens to us.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row" style="margin-top:20px">
        <a class="btn btn-2" href={platform.repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          View the source
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>What setting one up involves</b><span>Deliberate, not self-serve</span></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Organizations are provisioned by hand rather than by signup form. Your programs,
          their dates, the roles people hold and the boundary around your data are settled
          before a single student is invited, because all four are difficult to correct once
          students are working inside them.
        </p>
        <p>
          A sensible first step is one program: a single class or a single club season, with
          your real dates and your real students, while everything else stays where it is. The
          demonstration is the cheapest way to decide whether that is worth doing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec cta">
      <div class="sec-h"><b>Talk to us</b><span>A walkthrough takes half an hour</span></div>
      <div class="row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Request a walkthrough</a>
        <a class="btn btn-2" href="/try/">Open the demonstration first</a>
        <a class="btn btn-q" href="/for-educators/">For educators</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
